{"name":"Burnham","hex":"#234537","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Burnham","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A placename:\nA number of places in the United Kingdom\nA large village and civil parish in Buckinghamshire, previously in South Bucks district, and partly in Slough, Berkshire, England . \nA town in Essex, England; see Burnham-on-Crouch.\nA hamlet in Thornton Curtis parish, North Lincolnshire district, Lincolnshire, England .\nA coastal town in Somerset, England; see Burnham-on-Sea.\nA community in the Rural Municipality of Coulee No. 136, Saskatchewan, Canada.\nA number of places in the United States:\nA village in Cook County, Illinois, just south of Chicago.\nA town in Waldo County, Maine.\nAn unincorporated community in Howell County, Missouri.\nA borough in Mifflin County, Pennsylvania.\nA settlement in Canterbury, New Zealand, the location of an army camp. \nA park in Baguio, Benguet, Philippines.","A number of places in the United Kingdom\nA large village and civil parish in Buckinghamshire, previously in South Bucks district, and partly in Slough, Berkshire, England . \nA town in Essex, England; see Burnham-on-Crouch.\nA hamlet in Thornton Curtis parish, North Lincolnshire district, Lincolnshire, England .\nA coastal town in Somerset, England; see Burnham-on-Sea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Burnham"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burnham (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Burnham is a surname of English origin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnham_(surname)"},{"title":"Andy Burnham","blocks":[{"text":"Andrew Murray Burnham is a British politician who has served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom and Leader of the Labour Party since July 2026. He has been Member of Parliament (MP) for Makerfield in Greater Manchester since June 2026, and was Mayor of Greater Manchester from 2017 to 2026; before that he was MP for Leigh from 2001 to 2017 and held several Cabinet positions. Burnham identifies as a socialist and is associated with the Labour Party's soft left; he is also a member of the Co-operative Party, which is allied with Labour. His political ideology has been called \"Manchesterism\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andy_Burnham"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/500px-Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/1280px-Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/500px-Prime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrime_Minister_Andy_Burnham_portrait_(cropped_2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Andy_Burnham_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Andy_Burnham_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Andy_Burnham_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Andy_Burnham_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Andy_Burnham_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Andy_Burnham_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_